recorded in §7.35 (i): writing the prohibition into the draft creates a grep site for the
prohibited string by the same standard that clears the historical lines. Recorded rather
than chased -- rewording it to dodge the grep would weaken the prohibition to protect the
check, which is backwards. Check [9]'s ZERO-tolerance line is 'per-message attribution
established', which returns 0 as required.
